  "label": "Zombie is mapped as 'me' in the context of homophobia",
  "description": "The text 'gay people fear me' explicitly maps the zombie visual entity as 'me'. The zombie is positioned as the threatening entity that 'gay people fear', creating an analogical mapping where the zombie represents the speaker's self ('me') in the context of the meme's false claim about homophobia. This mapping is reinforced by the zombie's menacing posture and the text's framing of the viewer as the feared party.",
